  "semantic": [
    {
      "reason": "The frozen delta preserves the six-column representation and the fractional value of old timestamps (spec.md:17–35). The separate route returns 200 text/csv and uses the existing DomainError JSON handler (api.py:28–30,56–66). The account lookup emits 404 for an absent account (repository.py:10–18). The ledger encodes UTF-8 directly and uses a read session (service.py:55–62). The RFC 4180 writer emits a fixed header with CRLF, applies standard escaping, and writes original integer IDs and amounts, literal identifiers, normalized UTC timestamps and direction (history_export.py:110–129). Legacy parsing normalizes whole seconds in UTC and carries fractional digits separately, trimming only trailing zeros when producing Z output (history_export.py:62–95). The pinned no-network public HTTP probe confirmed UTF-8, CRLF, the header-only and 404 cases, quoted non-ASCII identifiers, exact integer amounts above 2^53, unchanged database contents, and equal stored and exported UTC instants for legacy rows. An independent HTTP precision probe replayed with and without a date filter and preserved the stored .654321Z value exactly. The entire tracked public suite independently returned 120 passes.",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-01",
      "verdict": "pass"
    },
    {
      "reason": "The delta specifies selection, exact-once ascending order, the type filter and inclusive UTC calendar dates (spec.md:43–62). Parameterized SQL selects each related integer ID once in ascending order and excludes unrelated transfers (repository.py:86–101). The incoming predicate excludes self-transfers, consistent with the outgoing label from the serializer (history_export.py:34–36). Strict calendar parsing rejects malformed or reversed dates and unknown direction with 422 invalid_export_query, returned through the shared JSON handler (history_export.py:39–59, api.py:28–30). The ledger applies the direction predicate and then independently compares both inclusive UTC date bounds without calculating an overflowing successor date (service.py:55–62, history_export.py:98–107). Tracked assertions cover self-transfers, both extreme dates, unpadded legacy years, and UTC offset conversion. The independent public HTTP probe confirmed one-sided and combined bounds, both calendar extremes, exact midnight and last-second inclusion, next-day exclusion, direction selection and stable query errors. The independent precision replay also selected the whole day correctly with a fractional last-second operation.",
      "requirement": "REQ-CSV-02",
      "verdict": "pass"
    }
  ],
  "version": 1
